                "quoted_status_profile_username": null,
                "reply_count": 13,
                "retweet_count": 28,
                "source": "Statusbrew",
                "text": "Let me tell you an interesting story about a bill called the Lower Costs, More Transparency Act, which passed the House in 2023 with 320 votes. Bipartisan. It forced hospitals and insurers to actually tell us what their prices are so we could start to figure out how to lower costs for patients.\n\nSounds like common sense, right? Lots of House support. So why wouldn\u2019t the Senate take it up?\n\nBecause the Senate was controlled by Democrats\u2014and the committee that handles healthcare was chaired by none other than Senator @BernieSanders.\n\nBernie refused to even bring the bill up for a vote.\n\nWhy? Because he *wants* the system to fail. The Left has said this openly many times. They\u2019ve always wanted a single-payer system, and they\u2019re willing to let the current system collapse to get it. What they want is a European-style socialist model\u2014one that doesn\u2019t innovate, doesn\u2019t compete, and ends up costing taxpayers more than we can possibly afford.\n\nSo when you realize these facts don\u2019t work in their favor, it suddenly makes sense why the CNN panel was so desperate to shout over me, interrupt, and mock me for coming prepared to take down their ridiculous narrative. \n\nWe have offered multiple solutions to lower costs. Democrats don\u2019t want to fix the source of these problems, they want to prolong them until the system finally collapses.",
